ittsburgh-population-growing"}, {"title": "2020 Census Data Shows Allegheny County Adds Population For First Time Since 1960", "url": "https://www.cbsnews.com/amp/pittsburgh/news/2020-census-data-allegheny-and-westmoreland"}, {"title": "www.publicsource.org", "url": "https://www.publicsource.org/?p=1225542"}, {"title": "Pittsburgh (USA)", "url": "https://citypopulation.de/en/usa/ua/usa/ua69697__pittsburgh/"}]}, "The 2020 census put Pittsburgh's population at 302,971. That was a 0.89% drop from its 2010 population, according to data released Thursday. The 2010 count was 305,704, per the Census QuickFacts table.\n\nThe decline slowed compared with the prior decade. It decreased by more than 8% during the 2000s.\n\nRacial composition shifted during the 2010s. The city's Black population fell by 13.4%, while the white population dropped 5.6% to 187,099. Meanwhile, the city's Asian population rose by 47%.\n\nAllegheny County, which contains the city, grew. It added more than 27,000 residents, its first population increase since 1960.\n\nFor the wider metro area, a city-population database lists the Pittsburgh urban area at 1,745,039 in 2020. It notes that urban areas are defined every 10 years using the previous census results, so that figure is not the metro population."], "durationSeconds": 5.8380469580000005, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01XbUpKb57cGsFxY87hXxa6x", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
